# React Native CLI (Mobile)

## Setup

- React Native **CLI** project — not Expo (no `expo-*` dependencies unless explicitly approved).
- TypeScript strict mode. Path aliases configured (`@/features`, `@/components`, `@/theme`).

## Feature structure

```
src/features/<feature>/
├── screens/
├── components/       # feature-private UI only
├── hooks/
└── index.ts          # public exports
```

## Design system

- **Centralized theme** in `src/theme/`: colors, typography, spacing, radii, shadows.
- All screens consume theme tokens — no hardcoded hex/spacing scattered across files.
- Shared UI primitives (`Button`, `Text`, `Input`, `Card`) live in `src/components/`.

## Screens & navigation

- Screens are thin: compose components, call hooks, handle navigation.
- Business logic and API calls belong in hooks (`useRentalAgreement`, `usePickupApproval`), not in screen components.
- Do not implement map views or map SDK integrations.

## Images

- Upload via presigned URL or multipart endpoint; display from object-storage URLs.
- Use `react-native-fast-image` or equivalent for caching — never store image binaries locally as persistence.

## Handover UX

- Owner flow: camera/upload for condition photos at pickup and return.
- Renter flow: view owner's submitted photos, approve or reject — **no camera for handover photos**.
- Show loading/error states; invalidate TanStack Query caches after successful actions.

## Performance

- FlatList for lists; memoize expensive list items.
- Avoid giant screen files — split into subcomponents when a screen exceeds ~200 lines.
